[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218055165","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109928#issuecomment-3218055165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109928","id":3218055165,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_z5_9","user":{"login":"gilzoide","id":4603360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4603360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide","html_url":"https://github.com/gilzoide","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-24T12:05:55Z","updated_at":"2025-08-24T12:05:55Z","body":"Interesting, after using this new build with Lua GDExtension I get the following error message:\r\n\r\n> ERROR: Required virtual method LuaScript::_instance_create must be overridden before calling.\r\n\r\nI guess const vs non-const affect virtual method resolution? So it seems this change could break existing `ScriptExtension`s. Not sure what's the best approach in this case. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3218055165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3232628374","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109928#issuecomment-3232628374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109928","id":3232628374,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Arf6W","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T09:08:56Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T09:08:56Z","body":"Const-ness is part of method hashes (which are compared during virtual call dispatch since Godot 4.4). Modifying the signature in a way that changes the hash constitutes a binary-breaking change in GDExtension.\r\n\r\nSince Godot 4.4 (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100674), there is a compatibility system for virtual methods, which would allow you to provide a migration path that doesn't break existing extensions. See also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92175 for an example.\r\n\r\nRegarding the change itself, I'm probably not the best to judge if it's necessary and worth the compat, hopefully others can jump in here :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3232628374/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3233303065","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109928#issuecomment-3233303065","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109928","id":3233303065,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AuEoZ","user":{"login":"gilzoide","id":4603360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4603360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide","html_url":"https://github.com/gilzoide","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T12:27:56Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T12:27:56Z","body":"> Since Godot 4.4, there is a compatibility system for virtual methods, which would allow you to provide a migration path that doesn't break existing extensions.\r\n\r\nOh, I didn't know of that, awesome! I'll rewrite it using this compatibility system when I have the time. Thanks for the tip!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3233303065/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235080230","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109928#issuecomment-3235080230","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109928","id":3235080230,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A02gm","user":{"login":"TitanNano","id":4500858,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA4NTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4500858?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano","html_url":"https://github.com/TitanNano","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TitanNano/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T22:02:15Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T22:02:15Z","body":"> These virtual methods should not be declared const to allow subclasses to cache these instances / placeholders and update them in _update_exports or ScriptLanguageExtension::_reload_all_scripts\r\n\r\nReloading scripts is indeed a bit of a headache due to these methods being `const` and therefore not being able to store any metadata for new script instances. \r\nIf this can indeed be achieved in a backwards-compatible way, then I think it would be a worthwhile change.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235080230/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3238295851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109928#issuecomment-3238295851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109928","id":3238295851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BBHkr","user":{"login":"gilzoide","id":4603360,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDMzNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4603360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide","html_url":"https://github.com/gilzoide","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gilzoide/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-29T21:17:08Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T21:17:08Z","body":"Ok, I added the compatibility methods and it seems to work pretty well, tested with Lua GDExtension!\r\n\r\nExisting GDExtensions should not be affected. Projects should still break when they update the extension_api.json to a version where the method is non-const, although I haven't tested doing that.\r\n\r\nNotice that I had to call the compatibility methods before the new ones, since they are required virtual methods. When I first tried the other way around, I would receive the \"Required virtual method ... must be overridden before calling\" error even though the compatibility method would run correctly afterwards.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3238295851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]